    LLM: 'Game: Kentucky Rook. Logic: bidding (min 100, multiples of 5), nest exchange, trump choice; trick points 1=15, 14=10, 10=10, 5=5, Rook=20; first to 500.',
    Player: 'Kentucky Rook: four players, fixed partnerships, 45 cards. Bid from 100, take nest, discard 5 (no point cards), name trump. Follow color; Rook highest trump. First to 500 wins.',
    objective: 'As the bidding team, take at least the number of card points you bid; as the opposing team, score the points you take. First team to reach 500 or more points wins.',
    gameplay: "Four in fixed partnerships. Deal 10 each, 5 to nest. Bid from 100 in multiples of 5 (left of dealer first); three passes leave the fourth as high bidder; if first three pass, dealer must bid 100. Bidder picks up nest (15 cards), discards five face-down (no point cards), names trump. Left of bidder leads; follow color; Rook is highest trump. Highest trump wins trick, else highest of led color. Bidder's team makes bid scores their points, else subtracts bid; other team always scores its points. Game to 500.",
